      "problem": "Calculate ${lim}_{x\\to 4}{log}_{5}⁡(4-x).$",
      "worked_solution": "Let's sketch the graph of $y={log}_{5}⁡(4-x).$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14273970/assets/4c8119ac59d4fe8102a4d78e10f32f1b3f0116366001b6a78d256b3928867943.png)\n\nThe function is not defined for $x\\ge 4.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to {4}^{+}}{log}_{5}⁡(4-x)=\\text{DNE}.\n$$\n\nHowever, the function is defined for $x<4.$ Moreover,\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to {4}^{-}}{log}_{5}⁡(4-x)=-\\infty .\n$$\n\nSince the left and right-sided limits are not equal, we have\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to 4}{log}_{5}⁡(4-x)=\\text{DNE}.\n$$",
